        "nobel_worthiness": "Atom interferometry brought matter-wave phase measurements into precision sensing, enabling sensitive measurements of acceleration, rotation, and fundamental constants while testing quantum coherence with massive particles.",
        "attribution": "Bordé developed foundational atom interferometry methods, while Pritchard and Kasevich advanced influential experimental implementations and precision measurements. The field's growth has involved many groups.",
